3. Content & Anti-Circumvention Boundary
----------------------------------------
- This repository contains ZERO copyrighted third-party binaries, `.ipa` files,
  firmware images, app icons, developer certificates, or decryption keys.
- This tool does NOT implement FairPlay decryption, CoreTrust exploitation, or
  any DRM/payment circumvention. Encrypted App Store packages (`cryptid != 0`)
  are explicitly rejected prior to installation.
- The built-in local userscript host (`:8787`) is a generic static script
  endpoint; no third-party userscripts are distributed in this repository.

4. Third-Party Projects Referenced (NOT Bundled)
------------------------------------------------
The following external projects are NOT included in this repository, but are
either runtime prerequisites, referenced research tools, or design inspirations:

- TrollStore (https://github.com/opa334/TrollStore)
  Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Lars Fröder — MIT License (RootHelper/uicache.m is
  BSD-4-Clause and is NOT included).
  Design & CLI interface inspiration only (RootHelper subcommand conventions in
  `src/fork/tsh`, `iTunesMetadata.plist` metadata lookup, System vs User
  registration distinction). No TrollStore source code is copied. See
  docs/zh/PORTING-TROLLSTORE.md and docs/en/PORTING-TROLLSTORE.md.

- TrollStore-tvOS (https://github.com/straight-tamago/TrollStore-tvOS) — MIT
  License (retaining upstream notices).
  Referenced in gap-analysis documentation for tvOS porting research only.

- Relaxin (https://github.com/owngoal-dev/Relaxin) — MIT License.
  RootHide-based tvOS 17 jailbreak providing `jbctl trustcache add` at runtime.
  Not part of this repository.

- roothide (https://github.com/roothide)
  Bootstrap / vroot framework used by Relaxin (`>= 0.1.0-5`). Not bundled.

- Procursus (https://github.com/ProcursusTeam/Procursus)
  Specifically `ldid` (https://github.com/ProcursusTeam/ldid) and `uicache`
  from `uikittools-ng` (https://github.com/ProcursusTeam/uikittools-ng),
  installed on the jailbroken device via APT; not bundled in this repository.

- vphone-cli (https://github.com/Lakr233/vphone-cli) — MIT License.
  Optional external macOS Virtualization.framework research tool referenced in
  documentation. Current latest-version limitation: its tvOS presets only
  support recent firmware around tvOS 26.6–27.x (~tvOS 27; tvOS 27+ requires
  macOS 27 host) and cannot boot tvOS 17.x. Not bundled.

